{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Third plan review 2026-10-18 (BLOCK, 1 move), confirmed against origin/main b97d414b8e2 and fixed:\n\n`docs/exit-codes.md:178` carries the per-command row for `enrich` (`| `enrich` | 0 | — | — | no ticket id; cross-ticket overlap drain; always 0 on a clean run |`). Removing the route without that row makes `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_exit_codes.py:304` report it as `orphaned` and fail `make verify`. The AC2 grep is scoped to `src scripts tests rebar.toml .rebar`, so it would not have caught a docs row. Scope now adds `docs/exit-codes.md` (drop `:178`), and the docs AC now also greps for a leading `enrich` table row and runs `test_exit_codes.py`.\n\nRunning tally for this story's reviews: 1st found 7 prose reference sites outside the edit list; 2nd found a wrong `fsck_scan.py` cite and a dangling `docs/README.md` link; 3rd found this orphaned exit-codes row. All were real; none changed the design."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1792368570692542604,"uuid":"c33827dd-75d3-4251-86c3-01553e090aa2"}